            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a planet, then the Gujarati for to make out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: મુહૂર્ત",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મુહૂર્ત — muhūrt — \"an auspicious moment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો સારું મુહૂર્ત હશે તો અમે રવિવારે નવા ઘરમાં જઈશું. jo sārũ muhūrt haśe to ame ravivāre navā gharmā̃ jaīśũ. If there is a good hour, we will move into the new house on Sunday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મુહૂર્ત (muhūrt) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit muhūrta, \"a moment, a short space of time\" (Monier-Williams); in Gujarati it is the right moment to begin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
