        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ચોઘડિયું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચોઘડિયું — coghḍiyũ — \"a choghadiyu (a lucky or unlucky part of the day)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો ચોઘડિયું સારું હશે તો દાદા સવારે દુકાન ખોલશે. jo coghḍiyũ sārũ haśe to dādā savāre dukān kholśe. If the time of day is lucky, my grandfather will open the shop in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચોઘડિયું (coghḍiyũ) is usually explained as built from co-, \"four\", and ghaḍī, an old unit of time, from Sanskrit ghaṭikā (Monier-Williams): the day is cut into such periods, each good or bad for beginning a task."
            }
          ]
        },
